Demography Module
Developer Description and Data Structure

Purpose. The Demography Module will provide a barangay-level demographic view of important community sectors.
It will allow staff to record the estimated or validated number of members belonging to each sector in every barangay.
The main objective is to help users understand the potential population affected or served when planning a program
for a particular sector.
1. Demographic Data Entry
Field Description
Barangay Select the barangay for which demographic information is being encoded.
Sector Select the applicable community sector.
Number of Members Enter the number of members belonging to the selected sector in that barangay.
2. Initial Sector Options
Sector
Fishermen
Farmers
Factory Workers
Entrepreneurs
Senior Citizens
Youth
Teachers
Important: The sector list must be configurable. Authorized users should have an Add Sector function so new
sectors can be added to the dropdown without requiring changes to the source code. Existing sectors should also be
manageable by an administrator.
3. Barangay Demographic View
When a barangay is clicked on the Mariveles map, the system should display the number of members recorded for
each sector in that barangay.
Sector Members
Fishermen 420
Farmers 185
Factory Workers 3,250
Entrepreneurs 610
Senior Citizens 1,150
Youth 2,800
Teachers 240

4. Sector-Based Map View
The user should also be able to select a specific sector from the dashboard. Once a sector is selected, the map
should show the number of members belonging to that sector in each barangay. This gives the user a geographic
view of where a sector is concentrated across Mariveles.
Example: If the user selects Fishermen, each barangay can display its fishermen count. If the user selects Senior
Citizens, the same map refreshes to show senior-citizen counts by barangay.
5. Program Planning Use
The demographic information is intended to support program planning. When planning a program for a particular
sector, the user can select that sector and immediately see the approximate number of people who may be affected
or potentially served in each barangay.
For example, a program intended for farmers can be viewed together with the number of farmers recorded in every
barangay. This provides a demographic reference for estimating program reach. The demographic count should be
treated as the recorded sector population, not automatically as the number of actual program beneficiaries.
6. Municipal-Wide Sector Summary
In addition to barangay-level figures, the system should automatically total the number of members in each sector
across all barangays. This provides both a Barangay View and a Municipal-Wide View.
7. Recommended Filters
Recommended filters are Barangay / All Barangays and Sector / All Sectors. Selecting a filter should immediately
refresh the map, sector counts, and demographic summary.
8. Core Data Logic
Barangay -> Sector -> Number of Members
The dashboard automatically generates Sector Population per Barangay + Total Sector Population
Municipality-Wide + Sector Distribution Across Barangays.
9. Recommended Data Management
Because demographic counts may change, the developer should allow authorized staff to update the number of
members. A Last Updated date is recommended so users can identify how current each demographic figure is.